# DockView asset editor tabs

New editor tabs for assets use **DockView panels** (`dockview-react` via `DockviewShell`), not a full-page workspace or shadcn `Tabs` as the document shell. Panels must be resizable, dockable next to each other, and able to host extra tabs later.

The toolbar **Windows** menu only works when the active document kind is in `DockviewDocumentKind`. If Windows stays disabled or omits a panel, the catalog wiring is incomplete.

## Required wiring

Do all of these in the same change:

1. Add the kind to `DockviewDocumentKind` / `DOCKVIEW_KINDS` in `apps/editor/src/shell/window-catalog.ts`.
2. Add a `DockWindowDefinition[]` (stable `id`, `component`, Title Case `title`, `defaultPosition` relative to a primary panel).
3. Register the `component` in `apps/editor/src/shell/panel-registry.tsx` (`IDockviewPanelProps`).
4. Implement panels under `apps/editor/src/panels/` with `PanelFrame` (omit a duplicate title when DockView already shows the tab name).
5. Mount `DockviewShell` for that kind in `apps/editor/src/components/document-workspace.tsx` and pass the **real** `documentKind` — do not fall through to the scene/graph branch.
6. Map the asset type in `documentKindForAssetType` (`packages/core/src/document.ts`).
7. Add `FOCUS_PRIMARY_PANEL` in `apps/editor/src/shell/layout-ops.ts`.
8. Cover the catalog in `window-catalog.test.ts`.

`WindowsMenu` lists `listDockWindows(kind)` automatically. `registerDockviewApi` persists placements in `layout.json`.

## Animation Graph exception

Animation Graph documents host a chrome **State Machine | Animation Object** `ToggleGroup` (`AnimEditorModeBar`) **outside** DockView. Below the bar, two stacked DockView surfaces persist separately (`layout.json` `{ animEditorMode, stateMachine, animationObject }`). The mode bar is **not** a dock tab. **Windows** and Focus follow the **active mode**. Nested shadcn `Tabs` still must not be the document layout.

## Do not

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — document shell is shadcn Tabs / AssetDocumentWorkspace
<Tabs>
  <TabsList>
    <TabsTrigger>Preview</TabsTrigger>
    <TabsTrigger>Details</TabsTrigger>
  </TabsList>
</Tabs>
```

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — Sprite-style catalog; Windows toggles these ids
{ id: "sprite-preview", component: "sprite-preview", title: "Preview" },
{
  id: "sprite-details",
  component: "sprite-details",
  title: "Details",
  defaultPosition: {
    referencePanelId: "sprite-preview",
    direction: "right",
    initialWidth: 280,
  },
}
```

- Do not hand-roll split panes or a new `asset-settings` kind for a full editor.
- Nested shadcn `Tabs` belong only inside **one** panel (mutually exclusive modes), never as the document layout.
- Content Browser stays a pinned chrome tab (not DockView). Existing compact Texture / Material / Model / Audio / Animation `asset-settings` stay until converted — do not add new types there.
